{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/635273-looking-for-character-advice-honoring-two-pantheons","id":635273,"title":"Looking for Character Advice: Honoring Two Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-21T18:04:18-07:00","id":635273,"title":"Looking for Character Advice: Honoring Two Pantheons","content":"I'm working on the story portion for my first Scion character, and I think that I've got a strong story despite the character starting out as a comics anti-hero ripoff.<br /> <br /> ~*~<br /> <br /> Jason Halson is the son of a Scandinavian diplomat that spent most of her time abroad in nations around the world. No one except his mother knew who his father was growing up, but something about Jason always seemed...off. He was always thin to the point of being bony, despite having an appetite that easily matched or exceeded those of other teenage boys, and seemed to have a fascination with blood and fire. He would sometimes order room service for a raw steak just to look at the blood and how it acted.<br /> <br /> Upon reaching adulthood, he set out on his own with nothing more than a motorcycle, the clothes on his back, and a rather substantial trust fund in a Swiss bank. He spent a few years just drifting, roaming the highways of North America as far north as Toronto, but something always called him back to Mexico City. It certainly wasn't the music or the tequila, but he could never figure out why he kept coming back.<br /> <br /> At the age of 25, he finally learned why after a bar brawl about fifty miles south of the Mexico-US border. Having knocked out a dozen men and so drunk he could barely stand, Jason was approached by a pale man in a suit that in his drunken haze looked remarkably like a skeleton.<br /> <br /> The man introduced himself as Mictlantechuhtli, his father. He explained that Jason was being recruited to fight in a war against the Titans and their spawn. To assist Jason in his fight, some of his personal effects were given a touch of divine power. A length of chain that Jason used to make sure that no one stole his ride would grant him the gift of Spirit-Sight and adjust its shape to any length. His Harley would never run out of fuel and travel swifter than any mortal machine. His leather jacket would serve as armor and render him impervious to fire and heat.<br /> <br /> ~*~<br /> <br /> Now for those that have not yet deduced who this character is based off of, that would be the Marvel Comics character Ghost Rider. My end-goal for Jason is that upon becoming a god his role amongst the Teotl is to serve as his father's bounty hunter. He hunts down and goes after those that have either escaped or are avoiding Mictlan.<br /> <br /> Given how I want him to still respect the gods of his mother's people, his cult would perform sacrifices for him in the manner known as the Blood Eagle. Cut open back, fold ribs away from the spine, flip lungs onto the shoulders, all while sprinkling salt on the open flesh. Adding to that, those that are sacrificed in this manner join him as he rides out to hunt those that are not in their correct Underworld, sort of a combination valkyrie/einherjar. If the Teotl allowed it, he would offer his bounty-hunting services to the other pantheons. &quot;What? Tantalus slipped out of Tartarus? Give me an hour, I'll have him back.&quot;<br /> <br /> My questions all boil down to, how would the Teotl feel about God-Level Jason? Would they be okay with the Blood Eagle since he is still taking sacrificial offerings or would they be outraged at him using a foreign ritual? Would they allow him to work with the other pantheons or want him to work exclusively for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T13:26:18-07:00","id":636227,"title":"","content":"In all honestly, probably no Pantheon is going to be <i>super-</i>happy about one of their members honoring foreign rituals and foreign Gods. Maybe less so in the Scion setting than historical reality would lead us to believe, since these Pantheons have to have diplomatic relationships with each other. In that way, it might not be so bad. But the Aztec weren't terribly friendly with non-Aztec cultures, and their Gods demanded an <i>incredibly</i> strict moral code from their followers. <br /> <br /> But could this new God make it work? Probably. If he invests in some Epic Socials, then certainly. Part of the whole fun of the new generation of Gods is that they can do stuff like this. They can make big changes, and create alliances that would be impossible for their parents to even consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T17:58:00-07:00","id":636514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/635273-looking-for-character-advice-honoring-two-pantheons?p=636227#post636227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...create alliances that would be impossible for their parents to even consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I now know how Jason will justify hiring his services out to the other pantheons. &quot;Look, if I get someone that managed to escape the Asphodel Fields then Hades owes me something in return. If someone sneaks out of Yomi and I return them, do you really think that the Kami are going to ignore me when I ask that they do something for us? The Aesir already like me because of the way I take my sacrifices, so I'm actually one of our best diplomats.&quot;<br /> <br /> Add in the fact that Socials was going to be one of his higher rated Attribute categories (maxed Monstrous Appearance, Charisma in the form of respect not love, with very little Manipulation &quot;Darn it John I'm a bounty hunter not a trickster&quot;) and I can actually see Jason being a decent diplomat in the form of getting the other pantheons to do stuff for him, and by extension his pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","user":"Meribson","date":". 08-22-2015, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}